{
  "method_card": {
    "steps": [
      "Order the data if finding the median",
      "For frequency tables: add an fx column (value × frequency)",
      "For grouped data: use class midpoints × frequency",
      "State 'estimated mean' for grouped data (midpoints give an estimate)"
    ],
    "title": "Averages & Spread",
    "content": "<p><strong>Mean</strong> = sum of values ÷ number of values. <strong>Median</strong> = middle value when data is ordered (position = \\(\\frac{n+1}{2}\\)). <strong>Mode</strong> = most frequent value. <strong>Range</strong> = largest − smallest.</p><p><strong>From a frequency table:</strong> Mean = \\(\\frac{\\sum fx}{\\sum f}\\). For <strong>grouped data</strong>, use midpoints: estimated mean = \\(\\frac{\\sum f \\times \\text{midpoint}}{\\sum f}\\). The <strong>median class</strong> contains the \\(\\frac{n}{2}\\)th value. The <strong>modal class</strong> has the highest frequency.</p>",
    "example": "<p><strong>Find the mean of 5, 8, 3, 12, 7.</strong></p><p>Mean = (5 + 8 + 3 + 12 + 7) ÷ 5 = 35 ÷ 5 = 7</p>"
  },
